    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Andy Pages** (73.47) serving as our primary engines for offensive production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a premium matchup against Chandler, where his dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable spot at the top of the order provide a high floor for both runs and average. Similarly, **Andy Pages** occupies a prime hitting environment against Sears; the combination of a high-xERA opponent and favorable wind conditions elevates his ceiling, making him an essential start despite the platoon neutral dynamic. **Gunnar Henderson** (69.41) and **Coby Mayo** (65.56) round out our top-tier targets, both drawing opportunistic matchups against Lodolo that should mitigate their platoon-related risks.\n\nRegarding our bench strategy, **Denzer Guzman** (44.48) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly falling behind our starters due to the volatility of facing Ranger Suarez. While his batting order slot is attractive, the current configuration of the outfield and infield rotations offers higher per-plate-appearance utility elsewhere. We have also opted to keep **Liam Hicks** (39.95) and **Josh Lowe** (37.17) sidelined, as both failed to clear the 40-point efficiency floor required to warrant a start in this Roto configuration. **Josh Lowe** remains a significant concern for our roster\u2019s stolen base targets, but his current projected efficiency against a tough lefty like Suarez makes him a defensive hold to preserve our limited game caps.\n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Heliot Ramos** (58.20), whose score is propped up by a massive +14% park factor and a situational boost for his elite sprint speed against a slow delivery pitcher. While his projection is solid, the risk remains moderate against Gordon. Additionally, while **Drake Baldwin** (52.57) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (52.75) are set to start, their matchups against McLean and Hancock carry higher SP risk than our top-end options; we are banking on **Drake Baldwin**'s BvP success to stabilize his performance. With **Jordan Westburg** confirmed on the IL, we are closely monitoring the rest of our depth\u2014including **Nasim Nunez** and **Brayan Rocchio**\u2014to ensure we maintain our competitive edge in SB as the week progresses.",
